slides.content:
# Use Sparingly

Adding `!important` to a declaration breaks the natural cascade and specificity rules:
```css
p {
  color: red !important;
}
```
It overrides any other declaration of the same property, regardless of specificity. Only use it as a last resort (e.g., utility classes or overriding inline styles). Overusing `!important` makes CSS unmanageable.
